[section:examples Examples]

The `examples/` directory contains complete, buildable programs that
exercise the most common use cases. The CMake target name matches the file
name minus the extension, e.g. `cmake --build build --target http_server`.

[table Examples shipped with the library
[[Example][What it shows]]
[[`awaitable_server.cpp`][Plain HTTP server with a handful of REST
 endpoints, demonstrating `path_arg`, `query_arg`, and a JSON-returning
 handler.]]
[[`chunked_server.cpp`][HTTP server that streams a chunked response from an
 async generator, useful for progress reporting or server-sent events.]]
[[`htdocs_server.cpp`][Serving a directory of static files with correct
 content types via `taar::handler::htdocs`.]]
[[`mixed_server.cpp`][Combination of REST handlers and a fallback
 static-file handler on the same session.]]
[[`response_stream.cpp`][Building a streaming response by hand, without the
 REST adapter.]]
[[`websocket_server.cpp`][Protocol upgrade to WebSocket via
 `register_raw_handler`.]]
]

Each example is small enough to be read top-to-bottom in one sitting. They
are the recommended starting point for a new application.

[endsect]
